# Hatch Tooltips
gt.blockmachines.hatch.nuclearbus.desc=Nuclear core bus for items\nHolds fuel rods, coolant cells, moderators, reflectors, insulators, radiovoltaics\nInput-only core component bus\nOutputs (depleted fuel) eject to output buses/hatches
gt.blockmachines.hatch.nuclearhatch.desc=Tiered nuclear fluid hatch (%s)\nHolds input coolant or liquid nuclear fuel\nInput-only core fluid hatch\nOutputs (steam, hot coolant, byproducts, depleted fuel) eject to output hatches\nCapacity: %s L\nCoolant boiling and transmutation under neutron flux\nConductance: %s Hu/(s·°C)\nItem pipe casing determines allowed coolants\nInserting coolant to dry hot hatches will damage hull!
gt.blockmachines.hatch.nuclearhighpressure.desc=Core pass-through endpoint for high-pressure coolant loops\nCoolant flows from top inlet to bottom outlet\nDoes not support standard-pressure fluid logistics!
gt.blockmachines.hatch.nuclearhighpressure.input.desc=Core pass-through top inlet for high-pressure coolant loops\nMust be placed on the top core layer (slice 0)\nPairs strictly with a bottom outlet hatch of the same material in the same column\nDoes not support standard-pressure fluid logistics!
gt.blockmachines.hatch.nuclearhighpressure.output.desc=Core pass-through bottom outlet for high-pressure coolant loops\nMust be placed on the bottom core layer (slice 4)\nPairs strictly with a top inlet hatch of the same material in the same column\nDoes not support standard-pressure fluid logistics!
gt.blockmachines.hatch.nuclearhighpressure.material=Material: %s (%s)
gt.blockmachines.hatch.nuclearhighpressure.capacity=Passage heat capacity: %d HU/°C
gt.blockmachines.hatch.nuclearcontrol.desc=Emits redstone signals based on nuclear reactor conditions\nRight-click with screwdriver to cycle metric (sneak+right-click for bundled mode)\nRight-click with soldering iron to cycle statistic\nOutputs 0-15 vanilla redstone or 0-255 ProjectRed bundled signals from front side\nSupports 16-channel ProjectRed bundled cables and OpenComputers interface
gt.blockmachines.hatch.nuclearcontrolrod.desc=Nuclear core control rod\nHolds long rods of silver, boron, cadmium, indium, or hafnium\nControlled by external redstone (0..15) or ProjectRed bundled cable (0..255)\nRight-click with screwdriver to cycle bundled input channel\nController SCRAM state overrides insertion to 100%!
gt.blockmachines.hatch.nuclearadvancedcontrolrod.desc=Dual-slot nuclear core control rod with moderator displacer\nSlot 0 holds a control rod; Slot 1 holds a moderator\nWithdrawing the control rod displaces the moderator into the core\nControlled by external redstone (0..15) or ProjectRed bundled cable (0..255)\nRight-click with screwdriver to cycle bundled input channel\nController SCRAM state overrides insertion to 100%!

